{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared","id":508398,"title":"Can hunters still be a thing to be feared?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-08T14:11:21-07:00","id":508398,"title":"Can hunters still be a thing to be feared?","content":"In Masquerade, it seemed a lot of what Vampires were afraid of were hunters. Even without crazy tech or powers, coordinated humans could be a massive threat during the daytime.<br /> <br /> It feels like, since 2nd edition Requiem vampires are most powerful white wolf vampires we've seen yet, that it'd be very, very hard for mortal hunters to be much of a threat. Certainly they could take a vampire out in the right circumstances, but they aren't the type of thing to strike fear into Kindred society at large like they used to be.<br /> <br /> What do you think? How afraid are Requiem 2nd ed vampires of hunters? Do you think that fear or lack thereof is justified? Are hunters a big threat in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T14:32:42-07:00","id":508425,"title":"","content":"All vampires still are out like a light during the day, can still be ambushed, can still be trapped in a burning down warehouse, lots of things to be afraid of. Not enough to be ALWAYS looking over your shoulder, but enough that a decent Hunter cell is still something to worry about and a poor one can still do some damage with some luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T14:39:21-07:00","id":508427,"title":"","content":"I think you wish to portray vampires in a flat out head on fight. Hunters, without military support, NEVER go head on. They set traps. They arrange situations. And they never ever hunt alone. A vampire can gut a normal human if the human pulls out a gun and opens fire. However, that same vampire would be hard pressed when they attack at 9 am by setting off explosives around the vampire's haven and then have several snipers setup a block away ready to open fire on the vampire the second he clears himself out of the rubble. And when the vampire tries to escape underground, then the vampire encounters the other part of the trap...namely some homemade napalm that would spill on the vampire when he crosses a certain section.<br /> These things? Easily done by normal humans in today's world.<br /> Now, if those hunters also have some backing or some supernatural support? Then the vampire is really screwed. So, should hunters be feared? YES! You should never ever disregard two things: humanity's tendency to unite against a common threat and humanity's ability to kill something when they really really really want to kill something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T14:40:29-07:00","id":508429,"title":"","content":"Well apparently in 2e there are now ways in which younger or very powerful vampires can survive direct sunlight exposure for short periods of time. A strong enough willpower can allow the vampire to remain active during the day, as well as various Disciplines, such as the Coils of the Dragon.<br /> <br /> Pretty much sunlight was one of Humanity's biggest advantages, but now that vamps have a partial resistance to it, that sort of tips the scales, since one well trained vampire is equal to an entire squad of humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T14:45:08-07:00","id":508432,"title":"","content":"If you're able to walk about in the sun during the day, you're either a high humanity, low blood potency Kindred or an Ordo Dracul Kindred with a lot of facility in the Coil of the Ascendant. The former is unlikely to have the capability to make him significantly stronger than humans in this situation, and might also be disadvantaged by Lethargy. The latter was probably going to kill them anyway unless they prepared for it.<br /> <br /> Let's also not forget the two other <i>really </i>important things: Fire and numbers.<br /> <br /> Hunters are absolutely as dangerous as they ever were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T15:57:58-07:00","id":508530,"title":"","content":"It depends on the vampire. Four hunters with handguns can certainly kill a vampire if they catch it off guard and it isn't especially combat focused. My preferred method is actually large vehicle drive bys. A SUV with five guys using SMGs can tear an unaware vampire to shreads.<br /> <br /> By that same token if the vampire has the right powers even fire doesn't work properly. Vampires with middle range Resilence can laugh off flamethrowers long enough to beat the wielder senseless. In my games I like to go with guerilla hunters. Since all weapons or of more or less equal effect against kindred these hunters travel in groups and use mundane weaponry (bats, boards, pipes, etc.) and try to jump a vampire as a mob to overwhelm them.<br /> <br /> Like alot of things in World of Darkness it really all depends on circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T16:36:27-07:00","id":508548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=508429#post508429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well apparently in 2e there are now ways in which younger or very powerful vampires can survive direct sunlight exposure for short periods of time. A strong enough willpower can allow the vampire to remain active during the day, as well as various Disciplines, such as the Coils of the Dragon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's based on Humanity and Blood Potency. Humanity determines how much damage you take from sunlight and Blood Potency determines the intervals at which you take the damage. Willpower doesn't really factor into it, and the Coil of the Ascendant works by temporarily lowering your effective Blood Potency. So only young vampires or those with a specific power can be active during the day, and even then they gain the Lethargic condition and are at real risk of just passing out. They won't fall asleep in the sunlight, but falling asleep during the day, outside of your Haven is still extremely dangerous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=508429#post508429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much sunlight was one of Humanity's biggest advantages, but now that vamps have a partial resistance to it, that sort of tips the scales, since one well trained vampire is equal to an entire squad of humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still one of their biggest advantages. And even without it, vampires still have a number of vulnerabilities that can be exploited. Stakes, fire, stakes on fire, and the fact that humans work together very well and vampires are usually at each other's throats all the time (even if they like to pretend they're not).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T17:26:26-07:00","id":508568,"title":"","content":"Even if vampires aren't entirely at each others throats, they're unlikely to share a haven unless they're particularly close. And the vampires who can stand a few moments of daylight still aren't exactly laying out on the beach, getting a tan while casually backhanding the heads off oncoming mortals.<br /> <br /> Sunlight and fire do aggravated damage, fire being probably one of the earliest technologies known to mankind. A stake through the heart can paralyze them, banes can be researched to cause more damage or hinder them in other ways, they rely on blood that can be spiked or simply taken away, their ghouls are great weak points.<br /> <br /> Vampires are powerful, but they are hardly unassailable, which is why they make an effort to hide themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T17:51:41-07:00","id":508594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=508568#post508568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if vampires aren't entirely at each others throats, they're unlikely to share a haven unless they're particularly close. And the vampires who can stand a few moments of daylight still aren't exactly laying out on the beach, getting a tan while casually backhanding the heads off oncoming mortals.<br /> <br /> Sunlight and fire do aggravated damage, fire being probably one of the earliest technologies known to mankind. A stake through the heart can paralyze them, banes can be researched to cause more damage or hinder them in other ways, they rely on blood that can be spiked or simply taken away, their ghouls are great weak points.<br /> <br /> Vampires are powerful, but they are hardly unassailable, which is why they make an effort to hide themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sunlight only does aggravated damage to lower humanity scores.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T18:12:11-07:00","id":508602,"title":"","content":"And if they have Resilience they can soak fire damage, but if you're talking about a high humanity elder of the Ordo Dracul who can ignore sunlight and fire you're just going to have to have smarter hunters with weapons other than the sun and torches.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://infinitecomix.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/The-Power-of-Teamwork.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-08-2015, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T18:47:07-07:00","id":508616,"title":"","content":"There was a play-test with an elder against a handful of SWAT and it was a challenge for the vampire. Multiple opponents mitigate singularly strong opponents. I don't think vampires worry much about a few hunters. The hunters would have to be very determined and patient. A dozen hunters would be a problem to deal with. A handful that come prepared would as well. I think most vampires try to avoid the notice of hunters so that is where the fear comes into play. Hunters do make nice direct opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T19:22:50-07:00","id":508634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=508616#post508616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple opponents mitigate singularly strong opponents.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the crux of it. Especially with the rarity of multiple attacks in 2ed, the vampire can at best hope to kill or otherwise disable 1 hunter in a round. In the meantime, the vampire is absorbing possibly hundreds of bullets from auto fire weapons. Even doing bashing damage, that could quickly add up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T19:28:48-07:00","id":508639,"title":"","content":"Let's also keep in mind that the scenarios Diggs is talking about is a SWAT Team going in blind. Hunters are pretty different beasts because they aren't just prepared, they're prepared to hunt monsters, and if they're fighting on &quot;even ground&quot; they're not very good hunters to begin with. They always should be trying to tilt the odds in their favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T02:53:52-07:00","id":508849,"title":"","content":"The minimum a lone hunter needs to end a vampire is a book of matches and an address. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T09:53:36-07:00","id":509064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=508568#post508568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if vampires aren't entirely at each others throats, they're unlikely to share a haven unless they're particularly close.</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't cotories share havens? Thought it was fairly common.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T10:06:35-07:00","id":509074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=509064#post509064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don't cotories share havens? Thought it was fairly common.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe extreme neonates, or perverts blood bonded to each other, but based on the fiction the most they have is knowing where a coterie-mate's haven is. In Damnation City, for instance, a vampire was late to a meeting so they went over and found the coffin he slept in nailed shut. In <i>A Hunger Like Fire</i>, when Persephone Moore told a friend about her new secret haven she went there and found they had bricked it up.<br /> <br /> Other exceptions could probably be found in Kindred who don't know any better or very close sires and their childer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-09-2015, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T10:53:07-07:00","id":509102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>andreamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=508634#post508634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the crux of it. Especially with the rarity of multiple attacks in 2ed, the vampire can at best hope to kill or otherwise disable 1 hunter in a round. In the meantime, the vampire is absorbing possibly hundreds of bullets from auto fire weapons. Even doing bashing damage, that could quickly add up.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Hunters are going in with bullets that is.<br /> <br /> They are more likely to go in with stuff that targets the Elder's Banes and either crossbows or even dragonbreath rounds.<br /> <br /> So your average cell is harmful to your health. A clued in cell is downright terrifying.<br /> <br /> Of course, this is assuming the cell is fresh and not having to slog through waves of minions.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T11:12:03-07:00","id":509121,"title":"","content":"Don't forget bombs. With the right knowhow, you can make some pretty effective incendiaries and explosives using easy-to-acquire ingredients... or so I've heard. With a big enough bomb, you theoretically wouldn't even need to locate a sleeping vampire's body, just the building in which its located. Of course, going this route is likely to get the hunter in trouble with more than just the local bloodsuckers.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite organizations from Hunter is Network Zero, a group less interested in killing supernatural monsters than in exposing them to the public. I would guess that the Invictus <i>hate</i> these guys: a bunch of upstart AV geeks with smart phones trying to undo centuries of careful secrecy. They're the kind of group that looks like an easily controlled annoyance, but could prove to be a terrifyingly real threat to the masquerade.<br /> <br /> If I ever get my Bay Area chronicle off the ground, those will be the mortals who keep local elders up during the day; enemy number one in the modern information war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T11:43:37-07:00","id":509132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=509121#post509121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget bombs. With the right knowhow, you can make some pretty effective incendiaries and explosives using easy-to-acquire ingredients... or so I've heard. With a big enough bomb, you theoretically wouldn't even need to locate a sleeping vampire's body, just the building in which its located. Of course, going this route is likely to get the hunter in trouble with more than just the local bloodsuckers.<br /> <br /> One of my favorite organizations from Hunter is Network Zero, a group less interested in killing supernatural monsters than in exposing them to the public. I would guess that the Invictus <i>hate</i> these guys: a bunch of upstart AV geeks with smart phones trying to undo centuries of careful secrecy. They're the kind of group that looks like an easily controlled annoyance, but could prove to be a terrifyingly real threat to the masquerade.<br /> <br /> If I ever get my Bay Area chronicle off the ground, those will be the mortals who keep local elders up during the day; enemy number one in the modern information war.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Cacophony tends to hound down and troll anything that breaks the masquerade on instinct or combine it with subgroups that can easily be dismissed as crazy. Invictus as a city based covenant, don't have the resources to go after the Network as a whole but the Cacophony really does their job for them. Just track the data leakage to the source if it is in their city and have a &quot;polite conversation&quot; with said person.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T15:50:40-07:00","id":509281,"title":"","content":"I could be wrong, but as I understand it the Cacophony is primarily an underground network that allows vampires to widely share news, rumors, and discoveries without drawing the attention of mortals. The Invictus, on the other hand, are called the &quot;Conspiracy of Silence&quot; for a reason - in theory, at least, the primary purpose of all their power-mongering and information peddling is that it allows them to shut down potential masquerade breaches before they happen... though the other perks don't hurt. In general they disapprove of the Cacophony, since it makes information about vampires more widely available, if in a carefully concealed context.<br /> <br /> In any event, the Invictus of the Mission (assuming you're using the published information about the Bay Area's vampires) are fairly unusual as far as local manifestations of the covenant go. They're noted for being more innovative, meritocratic, and technologically savvy than is typical for the First Estate, and specifically seem to have &quot;declared war on the internet.&quot; They embrace primarily researchers and workers involved in the information industry, and use a combination of web-based attacks, influence in the media, and agents planted in major tech companies in an effort to control the populace and keep them in the dark.<br /> <br /> You could weave any number of interesting stories around, say, a shadow war going on at the Google corporate campus between the Invictus and other interested parties (probably the Free Council, possibly the Barrett Commission and others) for control of the minds and souls of executives and developers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 05-09-2015, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T17:20:59-07:00","id":509312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=508849#post508849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The minimum a lone hunter needs to end a vampire is a book of matches and an address.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here's the thing with that type of strategy - how do you actually use it in play?<br /> <br /> It seems so many of the really wise hunter strategies just rely on never giving the vampire a chance (because if they get that chance, it is often game over for the hunters). This seems to make it really difficult to actually use them in an interesting way in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T17:47:20-07:00","id":509343,"title":"","content":"A hunter can drop a body at a haven and call the cops. A hunter can target a vampire's allies (touchstones) by kidnapping or a direct attack. A group of hunters can use a hail of bullets with or without bait to draw a vampire into a killing zone. As far as burning down the building a vampire is in, that is more for NPCs to get killed. There is no reason for hunter to stick with these &quot;really wise strategies&quot; anymore than a murderer would. The more complex the plan the easier it is to get caught. There is no way for a hunter to kill/destroy a vampire and not run into legal problems unless they can commit their actions without witnesses or a trace of evidence. Hunters won't generally use bombs or torch buildings. Hunters have to keep in mind nobody else believes in vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T20:18:00-07:00","id":509468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=509074#post509074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe extreme neonates, or perverts blood bonded to each other, but based on the fiction the most they have is knowing where a coterie-mate's haven is.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm... Core book vampire fiction, the little bits between chapters, seems to suggest that they lived together. And ran off together. I wouldn't call them extreme or perverts.<br /> <br /> I think the assumption that vampires are sleeping alone all the time to be problematic, especially with how 2e is handling vampires not instantly having hate-fear responses on sight. Not to mention that &quot;nests&quot; of vampires is a thing in hunter lore. So, from the vampire side, the PC party will likely be sharing a haven, given how the merits work. From the Hunter side, there's valid lore for facing an entire group of vampires instead of individuals.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, catch a cotorie asleep, or an individual, and its the same challenge (none). Hunters really need to focus on enemy weaknesses, or stick with tracking down less-than-full template baddies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-09-2015, 11:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T22:00:43-07:00","id":509578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=508429#post508429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well apparently in 2e there are now ways in which younger or very powerful vampires can survive direct sunlight exposure for short periods of time. A strong enough willpower can allow the vampire to remain active during the day, as well as various Disciplines, such as the Coils of the Dragon.<br /> <br /> Pretty much sunlight was one of Humanity's biggest advantages, but now that vamps have a partial resistance to it, that sort of tips the scales, since one well trained vampire is equal to an entire squad of humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>To go to the leading authority on the subject, Dracula had his hands full with Van Helsing and company despite having a whole plethora of vampiric powers and being able to walk about in the daytime unharmed by the sun\u2014and of them only Quincey Morris had any real martial bent. They made full use of the various banes he was susceptible to, and used organization, inside info, and teamwork to great advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3505,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","user":"Matt the Bruins fan","date":". 05-10-2015, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T23:58:25-07:00","id":509661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=509312#post509312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Here's the thing with that type of strategy - how do you actually use it in play?<br /> <br /> It seems so many of the really wise hunter strategies just rely on never giving the vampire a chance (because if they get that chance, it is often game over for the hunters). This seems to make it really difficult to actually use them in an interesting way in play.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You mean with vampire PCs targeted by hunters, or hunter PCs targeting vampires? <br /> <br /> For the latter, it's all a matter of running the hunter procedural with all the danger it poses and letting the players feel like smart badass monster hunters when they do it right. <br /> <br /> For vampires targeted by hunters, you can't just zap 'em, that would be boring. Player characters have an intrinsic resistance to being shot in the head from three hundred yards out without warning. There's always an unnecessary laser sight spotted at the last second, or a convenient pigeon flies by. The friendly neighbor's dog who inexplicably doesn't hate the vampire wakes him up before the fire gets to the crawlspace. Stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T01:37:58-07:00","id":509734,"title":"","content":"You run into the same problem you might with any antagonist. You want them to be smart, but you can't have them be too smart, or everyone comes to the table and you let them know their characters died when someone chopped off their heads while they were sleeping. So you balance off their intelligence with other things, like having them be nemeses of an NPC vampire, perhaps one the players are close to. Or interested in 'sending a message' that telegraphs their intent, like by targeting the players' minions first.<br /> <br /> Either way, hunters can be a viable threat. They can go brute force and just blow up your haven, leaving you to sun, fire, or however many tons of rock. Or they can go more subtle and attack your infrastructure and threaten your masquerade and feeding supply. Or they can go personal and shove your bane down your throat. Or any mix of those and a thousand thousand things more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=509468#post509468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm... Core book vampire fiction, the little bits between chapters, seems to suggest that they lived together. And ran off together. I wouldn't call them extreme or perverts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean second edition? Because it doesn't seem like they live together. They share a sire. One of them is still close to the sire, the other seems loyal but more distant.<br /> <br /> And having your own haven isn't a matter of the predator's taint, it's just survival and privacy. Sharing is certainly a thing vampires can do, but it seems to be the exception rather than the rule, based on the fiction between chapters and information about vampires and the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-10-2015, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T04:14:18-07:00","id":509776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=509734#post509734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean second edition? Because it doesn't seem like they live together. They share a sire. One of them is still close to the sire, the other seems loyal but more distant.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not the sisters - one was a neonate in a cotorie, and we don't know how the ancillae lived other than in a nice house. The survivor originally had a cotorie she lived with, knocked over trucks with drugs, went on a short nomad trip with before they all died.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">And having your own haven isn't a matter of the predator's taint, it's just survival and privacy. Sharing is certainly a thing vampires can do, but it seems to be the exception rather than the rule, based on the fiction between chapters and information about vampires and the books.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Exception rather than rule? Despite the default assumption that motleys share in their havens? That we have things like they House system? Before we start getting into daytime servants and ghoul guards? The new Lance &quot;granting sanctuary in my haven&quot; merit? The old Carthian justification for discount haven being &quot;we all live together more easily?&quot; I just flat disagree with you here.<br /> <br /> Before, vampires had issues living together because of Predator's Taint. Now? I'm not seeing any evidence of that. </span>There seems to be an overwhelming amount of suggestion that vamps aren't solitary anymore in my opinion.<br /> <br /> EDIT - As well, we need to consider this from a perspective of PCs. Are we a hunter cell attacking vampires? Or a cotorie of vampire PCs who may be attacked by hunters? Or are both groups NPCs? In the first scenario, we have whatever the ST wants for a challenge. Single vampire with revenant and ghoul servants (Neglatu for the win, love that bloodline)? Cotorie? Just plain alone? In the second, PCs often do bunk together, pooling their Haven; doesn't matter if they're the exception or if its standard, its what the ST has to consider. In the third? It happens in whatever method the ST wants, or is entirely glossed over because it doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-10-2015, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T11:16:39-07:00","id":510031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=509776#post509776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Exception rather than rule? Despite the default assumption that motleys share in their havens? That we have things like they House system? Before we start getting into daytime servants and ghoul guards? The new Lance &quot;granting sanctuary in my haven&quot; merit? The old Carthian justification for discount haven being &quot;we all live together more easily?&quot;</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Where does it say that there's a default assumption for coteries sharing their havens?<br /> <br /> Daytime servants and ghoul guards aren't vampires, giving sanctuary to a hunted vampire is very much an exception rather than a rule, that's why there's a merit for it, as is one covenant getting a special discount.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Before, vampires had issues living together because of Predator's Taint. Now? I'm not seeing any evidence of that. </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There seems to be an overwhelming amount of suggestion that vamps aren't solitary anymore in my opinion. </div> </div> </div>Show me. I'm looking through the book and I don't see any, and as I mentioned, the fiction I have seen suggests they don't. Even the one you're talking about doesn't suggest they sleep together, just travel together. One line, any book, stating that most Kindred share their havens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-10-2015, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T06:01:40-07:00","id":510568,"title":"","content":"Hunters can absolutely be threats. The hail of bullets is bad enough in groups, but even a lone hunter can get a few good shots in. After all, until Hurt Locker comes out the Combat Marksmanship merit is still in play, and any hunter worth his salt is going to have it; practical xp builds up fast. And then there's the fact that there are plenty of hunter groups out there that have their own special advantages or powers. Bringing any of their buddies that happen to get killed in a vamp fight back to life is a good way to make sure their numbers never really drop until a total cell wipeout. Wooden bullets that work like stakes let them nuetralize vampires from a distance. And then there's the Cainite Heresy. Those guys REALLY don't play fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5991,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","user":"Akaru","date":". 05-11-2015, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5991-akaru","name":"Akaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5991_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:50:57-07:00","id":511969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=509064#post509064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don't cotories share havens? Thought it was fairly common.</div> </div> </div> </div>In all the years I have played Vampire (Masquerade or Requiem), I NEVER saw a coterie (of player Characters) share a Haven. Not once. There just was not enough Trust.<br /> <br /> In my campaign city , I have One coterie of NPC's that tend to share haven. And that is it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:04:55-07:00","id":512031,"title":"","content":"I have seen maybe two or three vampires share a haven, but never a whole coterie. Everyone was pretty insistent on maintaining their own individual places when I ran Vampire a couple years back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:31:10-07:00","id":512052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=511969#post511969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In all the years I have played Vampire (Masquerade or Requiem), I NEVER saw a coterie (of player Characters) share a Haven. Not once. There just was not enough Trust.<br /> <br /> In my campaign city , I have One coterie of NPC's that tend to share haven. And that is it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Opposite boat here. Not only all my PCs used to share a haven as coteries, some NPC ones do the same","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:46:55-07:00","id":512071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=512052#post512052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Opposite boat here. Not only all my PCs used to share a haven as coteries, some NPC ones do the same</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. It just makes sense to pool your Haven dots. Though I see a lot more characters not sharing living space in 2e, now that it isn't three separate Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:52:43-07:00","id":512087,"title":"","content":"Players, especially 'starting' Kindred tend to be an exception to all sorts of standards.<br /> <br /> I don't think there's any vampires in the Chicago book who share a haven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:44:13-07:00","id":512219,"title":"","content":"I did mention a bunch of my NPCs doing the same? Especially young ones who are still in coteries? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Why wouldn't you share a haven? If it's trust issues.. well.. why are you in a coterie? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:55:12-07:00","id":512228,"title":"","content":"Most of my players have started with personal havens, and then added a communal haven separate from those for coterie use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:57:12-07:00","id":512230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=512071#post512071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same. It just makes sense to pool your Haven dots. Though I see a lot more characters not sharing living space in 2e, now that it isn't three separate Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh also... it sorta is? Safe Place can be pooled. Haven dots can be pooled as well, I think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T18:49:33-07:00","id":512448,"title":"","content":"Assuming you are roleplaying instead of rollplaying, I think it matters where they are from. In some cultures people are expected to have their own space. Others would find the solitude uncomfortable. To a lesser degree this is true of family size as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:10:29-07:00","id":512679,"title":"","content":"And a shared haven prohibits them from having their own space <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Nobody likes cramming inside a single room.. nobody forbids them from taking a place with enough space for each of them .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:09:46-07:00","id":512923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=512230#post512230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh also... it sorta is? Safe Place can be pooled. Haven dots can be pooled as well, I think?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean you don't have to buy Haven Size, Haven Security, and Haven Location all separately any more. Haven Size's function has been replaced by the Housing Equipment, and there are a lot of ways to acquire equipment so you don't have to dedicate XP specifically to having a big enough house any more. Haven Location's function has been replaced by Feeding Grounds, which is not conceptually tied to the Haven, and isn't pooled. Haven a Security's function has been replaced by Safe Place which does almost exactly the same thing. The new Haven Merit doesn't really have a 1e analogue, but works kind of like a more vampire-y version of Haven Security, but requires a Safe Place to be tied to. So now, if a character wants their own place to crash, they really only need one Merit (Safe Place) instead of two (Haven Size and Security). Haven is an option for added safety, but isn't required just to have enough living space or a lock on your door.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:35:04-07:00","id":512941,"title":"","content":"I dunno, my play group usually laughs off Hunters, because of the cotorie strength and Discipline awesomeness. My players noticed a mid-tier hunter cell was on to them, and went after the Hunters. Even if they only took a single hunter captive, a squad of 4 kindred have access to all sorts of ways to pry out secrets, even from unwilling minds. Hunters who opt to use fire and bombs risk bringing cops and possibly Federal attention down on themselves. Hunters have to be as quiet as their quarry, otherwise they'll end up locked up in a psychiatric ward, or going out in a blaze of glory.<br /> <br /> Unless the hunters are military grade, or otherwise well trained and ready for this sort of violence, which the vast majority aren't, a vampire with the same experience will win pretty easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:41:03-07:00","id":512949,"title":"","content":"I had four demons trying to take a piece of infrastructure(Not Vampire, I know, hear me out), when a gang of the Night Watch came in and started attacking the place. THeir only real advantage was Molotov cocktails and numbers.<br /> <br /> I completely chased them off.<br /> <br /> It's all in how you use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T09:13:50-07:00","id":512973,"title":"","content":"The real Hunter Killer in Vampire is Obfuscate (especially when combined with Celerity and BP 2+), not resilience. Unless they have clear-sighted or some other trickery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T09:37:21-07:00","id":513002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=512949#post512949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had four demons trying to take a piece of infrastructure(Not Vampire, I know, hear me out), when a gang of the Night Watch came in and started attacking the place. Their only real advantage was Molotov cocktails and numbers.<br /> <br /> I completely chased them off.<br /> <br /> It's all in how you use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'd say its a wee bit different because the offensive power of Demon runs the risk of calling in Angels. A vampire can use every aspect of their splat and fight back, Demons are kind of hamstringed (hamstrung?) in how they can fight back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:12:52-07:00","id":513389,"title":"","content":"Outside of a literal interpretation, yes a shared haven prohibits a person from having their own space. It's the &quot;share&quot; part. You can't kick everyone else out. You can't have locks and traps to protect you from <i>everyone</i> else. There are real people that want to live alone. They want to go to a home where they will not hear or see anybody else. There should be vampires like that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T09:09:29-07:00","id":514197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=513002#post513002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'd say its a wee bit different because the offensive power of Demon runs the risk of calling in Angels. A vampire can use every aspect of their splat and fight back, Demons are kind of hamstringed (hamstrung?) in how they can fight back.</div> </div> </div> </div>The principle still stands-it's all in how you use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T06:15:53-07:00","id":515099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=513002#post513002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd say its a wee bit different because the offensive power of Demon runs the risk of calling in Angels. A vampire can use every aspect of their splat and fight back, Demons are kind of hamstringed (hamstrung?) in how they can fight back.</div> </div> </div> </div> Demon, as a spy game, risk hamstringing themselves by breaking their Cover and not asking like a spy, drawing down the Authorities. In Mage, a mental game, you're punished via magical backlash that drives insanity and unpredictability. Promethean, a spiritual-survival game, made enemies via Disquiet. <br /> <br /> Vampire, as a social game, has primary social consequences. That doesn't make the consequences any less real for the bloodsuckers than it does for the rebel angels, constructs, or the wizards. With care, yes, you can get away with it. The same is true in Demon, Mage, Promethean, and any other game. Be careless in any game, and you hamstring yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T06:54:42-07:00","id":515113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=513389#post513389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of a literal interpretation, yes a shared haven prohibits a person from having their own space. It's the &quot;share&quot; part. You can't kick everyone else out. You can't have locks and traps to protect you from <i>everyone</i> else. There are real people that want to live alone. They want to go to a home where they will not hear or see anybody else. There should be vampires like that too.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its not a question of some vampires wanting to be alone. Its a question of what the norm is. No one will argue that the norm for a werewolf is the pack, and yet we still have a notable number of lone wolves. That some will be alone, and some in a group, was never in doubt. Its a question of what percentages.<br /> <br /> If a hunter breaks into a vampire's haven, will they generally find a group of some kind, or a solitary? <br /> <br /> I've actually started to consider it an academic question that's only answer is &quot;It depends on what the ST and individual players want.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=512941#post512941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, my play group usually laughs off Hunters, because of the cotorie strength and Discipline awesomeness. My players noticed a mid-tier hunter cell was on to them, and went after the Hunters. Even if they only took a single hunter captive, a squad of 4 kindred have access to all sorts of ways to pry out secrets, even from unwilling minds. Hunters who opt to use fire and bombs risk bringing cops and possibly Federal attention down on themselves. Hunters have to be as quiet as their quarry, otherwise they'll end up locked up in a psychiatric ward, or going out in a blaze of glory.<br /> <br /> Unless the hunters are military grade, or otherwise well trained and ready for this sort of violence, which the vast majority aren't, a vampire with the same experience will win pretty easily.</div> </div> </div> </div> You know, when talking about using humans as enemy opponents for a supernatural, I feel like we're talking about a Hunter: the Vigil cross-over. Not sure how much I like that. I like my vampire hunters to organically rise out of mistakes that the characters make with the Masquerade. That holds true for all the games, really. The feeling that we have the Night Watch already established and just waiting for a hint to send humans after vampires isn't necessarily something I want in a Requiem game. That's what rogue ghouls and VII are for, imho. At least, that's what I use them for in my games. Something tied more intimately to the vampire condition.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:08:57-07:00","id":515120,"title":"","content":"I strongly agree with that stance on hunters, MCN. In my games hunters serve as the ultimate consequence of ignoring the Masquerade. Elders get pissy because you've broken the law, the Invictus will come down on you to protect the status quo. But the status quo is there for for a reason, and it's because there are so many more humans who can move around during the day at no disadvantage. <br /> <br /> Even vampires who can walk in the sunlight can only manage it briefly, and they're still at less than full capacity. If the 800 lb. gorilla that is the mortal herd gets wind of the predators in their midst they band together, apply ingenuity, and do one of the things that humans do best: Wreck shit.<br /> <br /> Daysleep is a cold, hard bitch, and it's still a huge level to the playing field.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T12:08:28-07:00","id":515333,"title":"","content":"I consider it an academic question, as you put it, MCN. That was my purpose. There are no known percentages except in a particular city, therefore what the group decides. A hunter that breaks into a haven should not know what to expect. There might be one very powerful vampire or a handful of vampires or a brood. Haven merits work best for NPCs. For players, they are just flavor because the truth is all the defenses can be overcome when it works for the story. If players feel they <i>need</i> to band together to have the best defenses in the world then they have an antagonistic relationship with their ST. If players have characters that feel they need to band together for mutual defense then that would be the norm for that particular setting, extremely dangerous. Is that every setting? No. The number of vampires in a haven will be determined by covenant, city, and age of the vampires. We could probably agree on some relative details, but there is no real reason for vampires to share a haven unless they wanted. The ratio is then undefined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T09:11:03-07:00","id":518146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/508398-can-hunters-still-be-a-thing-to-be-feared?p=508602#post508602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if they have Resilience they can soak fire damage, but if you're talking about a high humanity elder of the Ordo Dracul who can ignore sunlight and fire you're just going to have to have smarter hunters with weapons other than the sun and torches.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://infinitecomix.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/The-Power-of-Teamwork.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's assuming the hunters survive the initial encounter and realize the vampire can do that stuff. And yeah, Resilience has the ability to soak aggravated damage, which makes a level 5 Resilience master very difficult to injure.<br /> <br /> On the subject of Ghouls being a weak point, vampires can turn anybody into a ghoul. Doesn't even have to be human, just feed a stray dog your blood and suddenly you've got a hellhound, which is more vicious, faster, and loyal than a human Ghoul ever is. Imagine a trained attack dog come running at you with a Celerity boost or Potence as they wrestle you to the ground and start tearing chunks out. Or a particularly eccentric Gangrel decides he wants to Ghoul a chimpanzee!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But I'd say hunters can not only be deadly opponents, but also terrifying. They're united by hatred, hatred that is directed towards you, the vampire!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T17:02:17-07:00","id":520206,"title":"","content":"Personally the greatest weakness humans face, in my opinion, is during the intelligence gathering stage. Okay, so IF they find the vampires' haven they can win, right? Except they have to find out where a notoriously secretive creature is sleeping without giving themselves away. So you have to first learn how to trail after them and if you give yourself away, they only need a dot of Dominate, Obfuscate, Animalism or Majesty to get you where they want you (in the middle cases following you home) and then blood bonding you into servitude. So unless the hunters want to publicly splash someone with fuel and set them alight (a risky proposition in most spots as cops tend to frown on it), they're going to have to coordinate a surveillance effort that requires a lot of training against regular humans who can't see perfectly in anything but pitch blackness. Unless you're going with well-trained Vigil Hunters, this is not likely to be a skill that they start off having while it is something that those paranoid vampires should quickly develop (in terms of spotting a tail) since their vampiric enemies are just as keen to know where they sleep.<br /> <br /> So you've got a creature that can see much better in the dark than you can, whose heartbeat can give away their hiding place if the vampire passes through a couple meters (and if they're female, possibly a couple dozen yards depending on your time of the month), whose blood can enslave you and cause you to give up your allies (even the first level of blood bond makes it a Breaking Point at 5 to let them get hurt), and who have several disciplines that allow for fantastic levels of surveillance to follow you. Dominate can be used in combat to turn one against the others, Obfuscate makes them hard to notice, Protean lets them disappear into the soil, Celerity lets them seemingly disappear (if they end up behind cover you won't know where they went) and Resilience makes even fire lack much of a punch. Also all damage dealt to them is bashing unless it's fire or sunlight. Oh, and unless it's aggravated damage, the vampire can spend blood to heal up the damage those hunters are laying on. And if they frenzy, they add their BP to all combat rolls.<br /> <br /> And sunlight? Well, if they have low BP and high Humanity (which means up to 100 years old if they have regular BP), they can survive ten minutes in the sun which is more than enough time to kill everyone and go hide in the fridge until nightfall.<br /> <br /> On the other side, you have a group of humans who take lethal from everything other than fists, pass out if they fill up with bashing, can be blood bound into giving up their friends within three nights (and may not even need to be kidnapped if a coterie-mate with blush of life spikes their coffee), and can't see very well in the dark. And that's not adding in the difficulties of getting heavy duty firepower or high level combat, surveillance and counter-surveillance skills. Also, if the human is injured they wear it longer and may even need medical help -- which raises questions and can draw the attention of the authorities if they have stab or bullet wounds. Finally, the larger the team the harder it is to stay hidden and keep a secret. Plus the odds of a single breach convincing a half dozen humans who know each other to risk their lives and fight back are pretty low and any attempts to find other hunters to group up with risks them coming to the attention of other hunters. So you're probably looking more often at two, maybe three, hunters rather than six to eight. <br /> <br /> Even a relatively weak vampire can take enough punishment from two to three hunters and grind them down in return.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}